---------------------------Netpbm: a toolkit of small single-purpose programs that convert between imageformats by way of a common intermediate -- PBM (bitmap), PGM (greyscale), PPM(colour), collectively PNM.  Nothing here is interactive and nothing draws onyour screen; each reads one format on stdin and writes another on stdout, sothey are meant to be piped:    giftopnm < picture.gif | pnmscale 0.5 | ppmtopgm > small.pgmKept in their own directory because 169 near-identically named converters in/dd/CMDS would bury everything else.These formats convert out of PNM and back with the difference zero pixelfor pixel: xbm, icon, ybm, g3, macp, cmuwm, mgr, atk, gem, gif, pcx, bmp,tga, sgi, rast, ilbm, xpm and rgb3.  A few notes:  ppmnorm, pnmtosir, ppmtoxpm, xpmtoppm and pbmtext each carry a 64k  stack.  fstopgm, hipstopgm, imgtoppm and xvminitoppm print a diagnostic  when handed a format that is not theirs.  pnmtosir/sirtopnm come back the right size with the channels rotated  over the first half of the pixels -- a solid red 4x1 returns as green,  green, red, red -- so for a round trip use another format.ppmtopict/picttoppm round-trip exactly -- PICT joins the list above.picttoppm warns `can't load font directory' and converts anyway.  ppmtoyuvsplit/yuvsplittoppm round-trip the size but not the pixels,  which is the format itself: 4:2:0 chroma subsampling keeps one  luma byte per pixel and one chroma pair per 2x2 block, so a 32x16 image  gives .Y = 512 bytes and .U = .V = 128.  ppmtoyuvsplit takes a base name  and writes three files in the data directory, not to standard output.  sputoppm reads any bytes as an Atari Spectrum 512 picture and writes a  320x200 PPM -- the format is a fixed size with no magic number to check,  so unlike the nineteen converters that answer `not a <format> file' it  accepts anything.  imgtoppm writes nothing for a format that is not  its own.  pbmtobbnbg rejects the PBM bitmaps this disk's netpbm makes, raw or  plain, with `bad magic number - not a pbm file'; the other PBM  converters read the same files.  Into the PNM formats (49)  asciitopgm     reads a text picture -- ASCII art -- as a greymap, each                 character's darkness a grey level  atktopbm       Andrew Toolkit raster to PBM  bioradtopgm    Bio-Rad confocal microscope image to PGM; -image picks one                 of a stack  bmptoppm       Windows or OS/2 BMP to PPM  brushtopbm     Xerox doodle brush to PBM  cmuwmtopbm     CMU window manager bitmap to PBM  fitstopnm      FITS, the astronomers' image format, to PNM; -image picks a                 plane, -min and -max set the scaling  fstopgm        Usenix FaceSaver image to PGM  g3topbm        Group 3 fax file to PBM  gemtopbm       GEM .img (Atari and PC) to PBM  giftopnm       GIF to PNM; -image picks one of several in the file,                 -comments prints its comments  gouldtoppm     Gould scanner file to PPM  hipstopgm      HIPS, the image-processing package's format, to PGM  hpcdtoppm      Kodak Photo CD image to PPM, at one of five resolutions  icontopbm      Sun icon to PBM  ilbmtoppm      Amiga IFF ILBM to PPM, HAM and extra-halfbrite pictures                 included  imgtoppm       Img-whatnot, a PC paint program's format, to PPM  lispmtopgm     Lisp machine bitmap to PGM  macptopbm      MacPaint to PBM  mgrtopbm       MGR window-manager bitmap to PBM  mtvtoppm       MTV or PRT ray-tracer output to PPM  pcxtoppm       PCX, PC Paintbrush's format, to PPM  pi1toppm       Atari Degas .pi1 to PPM  pi3topbm       Atari Degas .pi3 to PBM  picttoppm      Macintosh PICT to PPM  pjtoppm        HP PaintJet file to PPM  pktopbm        TeX packed-font (.pk) characters to PBM, one bitmap per                 character  psidtopgm      a PostScript image -- the hex data of an `image' operator --                 to PGM, given its width, height and bits per sample  qrttoppm       QRT ray-tracer output to PPM